# What the build context is allowed to contain (#531).
#
# Everything is excluded and `web/` is put back, rather than the other way
# round, because this repository holds two things a build context must never
# pick up and both live outside `web/`: `.git`, which carries every revision of
# everything, and `.claude/worktrees/`, which holds other agents' checkouts of
# this same repository. A deny list would have to keep naming them; this way an
# addition at the root is out by default.
#
# The one cost is that a new build input outside `web/` has to be re-included
# here on purpose. That is the intended cost.
*
!web

# And inside `web/`, the things that are made rather than written. `dist/` and
# `dist-server/` are built inside the image; `node_modules/` is installed there,
# and copying a Windows tree in would put the wrong compiled addons next to the
# right ones. `data/` is a developer's scratch catalogue and its photographs.
web/node_modules
web/dist
web/dist-server
web/data
web/.scratch-*
web/*.traineddata
web/*.local
